.TH "zelta\-unlock" "8" "" "" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]zelta unlock\f[R] \- unlock a dataset tree for Zelta promotion
workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]zelta unlock\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]endpoint\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]zelta unlock\f[R] reverses the lock state used by Zelta promotion
workflows so a promoted dataset tree can become active.
It is a lower\-level companion to \f[B]zelta failover\f[R] for operators
who need to script each step explicitly.
.PP
Most users should start with \f[B]zelta\-failover(8)\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Unlock a promoted standby tree:
.IP
.EX
zelta unlock standby.example.com:tank/service
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non\-zero on error.
